WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.450
In April 2018, the UK put a new tax

2
00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:05.450
on sugary soft drinks.

3
00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:08.530
Drinks with 8 grams of
sugar or more per 100

4
00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:11.930
millilitres paid 24 pence a litre.

5
00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:14.330
Under 5 grams: nothing.

6
00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:16.410
Would it cut the sugar people drink?

7
00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:19.450
Or would it mostly raise
money for the government?

8
00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:23.190
So can a tax on sugary
drinks make people healthier,

9
00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:25.160
or does it just raise money?

10
00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:27.810
In this mission, you'll
draw a tax on a supply

11
00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:31.110
and demand diagram and watch a curve move.

12
00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:33.260
Then you'll set the tax yourself,

13
00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:35.600
in two very different drink markets,

14
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.840
and see what happens to sales.

15
00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:42.040
Your mission: find out when a
tax changes what people buy,

16
00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:44.120
and when it mostly raises money.
